# RV-OPS-13 / IN-02: build context of the Python image (Dockerfile: api, bot,
# scheduler, migrate). It is an allowlist: Docker anchors patterns at the
# context root, so a denylist such as `*.md` or `.env` missed nested files
# (reviews/, api/.env, bot/local.db, ...) and every new untracked directory.
# Only what the Dockerfile COPYs and `uv sync` builds gets in: pyproject.toml,
# uv.lock, README.md (the package readme declared in pyproject.toml),
# .python-version and the api/, bot/, scheduler/ and migrations/ packages.
# Dockerfile.frontend has its own allowlist in Dockerfile.frontend.dockerignore,
# which BuildKit reads instead of this file for that build.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!.python-version
!api/
!bot/
!scheduler/
!migrations/

# Inside the allowed packages: secrets, local databases, notes and caches stay
# out. NEVER bundle .env into an image: values come from the compose
# environment at run time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.dump
**/*.md
!README.md
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
